<!--
    kuna option bejoin evidence (the default), GH-904: a long long read from
    memory, or handed back by a call and moved back into r3:r4, joins high
    word first.

    PowerPC returns a long long in r3:r4 with the HIGH word in r3.  Joined
    first register low (option bejoin off, upstream's join), a long long
    loaded from memory printed with its words swapped:
        ld_ll:  return CONCAT44(a0->field_0x4,a0->field_0x0);   (bug)
    and a function returning a proven callee's long long it kept across
    another call read the call high word first but its own return low word
    first:
        carry_ll:  return CONCAT44((int4)v1,(int4)((uint8)v1 >> 0x20));   (bug)
    The evidence walk now also proves a pair that holds two loads of
    adjacent words of one object, the high word at the lower address, the
    low word read by nothing else (an int that returns one word of a
    non-volatile 64-bit object never loads the other), and a pair one direct
    call handed back whose callee is proven, when the function moved the low
    word back into r4 itself (an int returning the high word keeps only r3
    across ext()).

    Stage: P4 calls and prototypes (output-prototype), option bejoin.
    Pass 1 is the default (evidence), pass 2 option bejoin off.

    Source (gcc 13.3 -O2 -fno-pic -c, target powerpc-linux-gnu, linked at
    0x10000000 with -nostdlib -static, .text):
        typedef long long i64;
        struct S { int a; int pad; i64 v; };
        __attribute__((noinline)) void ext(void) { __asm__ volatile(""); }
        __attribute__((noinline)) i64 wid(int x) { ext(); return x; }
        i64 ld_ll(const i64 *p) { return *p; }
          lwz r4,4(r3) / lwz r3,0(r3) / blr
        i64 ldfield_ll(const struct S *s) { return s->v; }
          lwz r4,12(r3) / lwz r3,8(r3) / blr
        i64 carry_ll(int x) { i64 v = wid(x); ext(); return v; }
          bl wid / mr r30,r3 / mr r31,r4 / bl ext / mr r3,r30 / mr r4,r31 / blr
        int carry_hi(int x) { i64 v = wid(x); ext(); return v >> 32; }
          bl wid / mr r31,r3 / bl ext / mr r3,r31 / blr
        int ld_sum(const int *p) { return p[0] + p[1]; }

    Asserts #1-#2: the default returns ld_ll's and ldfield_ll's long long
      whole; off keeps each swapped.
    Assert #3: the default reads carry_ll's call and returns it in the same
      order (r3 high); off joins both first register low.
    Assert #4: carry_hi reads the high word of wid's long long in the
      default, and stays an int in both passes.
    Assert #5: ld_sum stays an int in both passes.
-->
